TASK 2 – GREEDY vs DYNAMIC PROGRAMMING
Build It, Break It, Explain It (9 Marks)
Programming Language: Python
Algorithms:
- Solution A – Fractional Knapsack using Greedy Strategy.
- Solution B – 0/1 Knapsack using Dynamic Programming.
1. Problem Analysis
A logistics company has a vehicle with limited carrying capacity. Each item has an Item ID, Weight and Value.

The objective is to select items to maximize the total value without exceeding the vehicle capacity.

Value-to-weight ratio:
\[
Ratio=\frac{Value}{Weight}
\]

The two methods work differently:
Fractional Knapsack	0/1 Knapsack
Uses Greedy strategy	Uses Dynamic Programming
Items can be divided	Items cannot be divided
Selects based on value/weight ratio	Considers different combinations
Can take a fraction of an item	Takes the whole item or rejects it

2. Source Code – Both Implementations
The following program implements both algorithms and displays the selected items, decision sequence, operation counts and memory requirements.
