2.2 Break the Greedy Intuition (3 Marks)
Now consider the same dataset, but change the requirement:

Items cannot be divided. Each item must be selected completely or rejected.

This is the 0/1 Knapsack problem.
Greedy 0/1 implementation
Add the following function to the previous Python program. It applies the same value-to-weight ratio strategy but selects only complete items.
def greedy_zero_one(items, capacity):    sorted_items = sorted(        items,        key=lambda x: x[2] / x[1],        reverse=True    )    total_value = 0    total_weight = 0    selected = []    print("\nGREEDY 0/1 KNAPSACK")    for item_id, weight, value in sorted_items:        ratio = value / weight        if total_weight + weight <= capacity:            selected.append(item_id)            total_weight += weight            total_value += value            print(item_id, "Selected | Ratio:", ratio)        else:            print(item_id, "Rejected | Ratio:", ratio)    print("Selected Items:", selected)    print("Total Weight:", total_weight)    print("Total Value:", total_value)    return total_value



