Why does Greedy fail?
- First commitment: Greedy selects item A because it has the highest ratio.
- Second commitment: It selects item B.
- Remaining capacity is 20 kg.
- Item C weighs 30 kg, so it is rejected.
- The total value is only 160.
The first greedy commitment to item A prevents the optimal combination A from being replaced by the more valuable combination B and C.
