2.3 Engineering Comparison (2 Marks)
Comparison	Greedy Fractional	Greedy 0/1	DP 0/1
Strategy	Ratio sorting	Ratio sorting	Table-based optimization
Sorting	Required	Required	Not required
Main operations	Item decisions	Item decisions	153 DP states
Time complexity	\(O(n\log n)\)	\(O(n\log n)\)	\(O(nW)\)
Auxiliary space	\(O(n)\)	\(O(n)\)	\(O(nW)\)
Solution quality	Optimal	Not always optimal	Optimal
Item division	Allowed	Not allowed	Not allowed

Here, n represents the number of items and W represents the integer vehicle capacity.

Engineering observations:
1. Computational work: Greedy sorts the items and makes quick selection decisions. DP evaluates 153 states for the three-item, 50-capacity example.
2. Memory requirement: Greedy requires storage for sorted items and selected items. DP stores a two-dimensional table containing (n+1) × (W+1) entries.
3. Solution quality: Fractional Greedy achieves 240, while Greedy 0/1 achieves only 160. DP 0/1 achieves 220.
4. Optimality guarantee: Fractional Greedy is optimal for fractional knapsack. DP guarantees the optimum for 0/1 knapsack with integer weights and capacity.
